# CR 305: playing a land is not casting a spell -- no cost, no stack, one
# per turn. Untap -> Upkeep -> Draw -> Main1, then playland moves the Plains
# from hand to the battlefield and counts it against the turn's own limit,
# and CR 305.6's own intrinsic mana ability (TapLandForMana) works on it
# immediately, the same turn -- a land is summoning-sick for combat and
# tap abilities that need it, but tapping a land for its own basic mana is
# not a tap ability with a summoning-sickness restriction (CR 302.6 only
# restricts a creature's own tap abilities).
startturn human
advance 3
playland human 1
tapformana human 1 W
paymanacost human W
